WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.510
- [Kelly] So wait, you recently
called the first round,

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:05.070
Single Jeopardy, instead of just Jeopardy.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.870
So, how did people react to that?

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.400
- So the,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.770
on my, I have basically,

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.700
clue boards that I review.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.060
- Yeah.
- And the first one does say,

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:14.893
Single Jeopardy,

00:00:14.893 --> 00:00:15.726
and the second one says,

00:00:15.726 --> 00:00:16.559
Double Jeopardy.

00:00:16.559 --> 00:00:19.200
So, I didn't make something
up that doesn't exist.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.510
And people though, lost their minds.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.020
So we usually call it the Jeopardy round.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.150
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And yes,

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.020
one time we were going,

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.550
I think to commercial and,

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.500
I think the thing that I'd
like people to remember is

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.640
I don't go rogue.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.270
It's never like, "What
is Mayim Bialik saying?"

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.940
There's 86 people watching what I'm doing.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.820
If they wanted me to redo it,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.390
I would've been happy to redo it,

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:41.460
but no one said anything.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.480
I just kept talking.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.313
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:43.313 --> 00:00:44.146
- But I won't do it again,

00:00:44.146 --> 00:00:47.710
'cause it caused a whole
Jeopardy viral situation.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.050
- Oh my God, just so you know,

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.713
I think my team gets
nervous because I go rogue.

00:00:51.713 --> 00:00:53.000
(both laughing)

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.740
- I, no with Jeopardy,
I'm very party line.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.910
Like they're in my ear, I read
the thing, I do the thing.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:00.780
But obviously that one slipped by.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.950
- Isn't it funny what
people freak out about?

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.560
- People care a lot about Jeopardy

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.180
and that's very important.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.520
- I know, it is important,

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.040
but you almost wanna just like,

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.840
start sending them, like real things

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.390
that are happening that are important.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:15.040
And you're like, you know,
like don't even respond.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.370
Just respond with like, I don't know,

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:18.570
there's a lot of homeless people here

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:19.640
we should probably look out for.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.310
Or, I don't know,
there's like real issues,

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.382
and I'm always like--

00:01:24.382 --> 00:01:25.215
(audience clapping)

00:01:25.215 --> 00:01:26.930
Why did you focus on that?

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:28.010
I don't understand,

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:28.843
but whatever.

